+section('updates py-3', 'insight-inside')
    .row
        .col
            +title('mb-4','Inside Qatar')
            p.fs-20.fw-medium.text-secondary.mb-4 Qatar Deepens Global Economic and Strategic Ties
            p.fs-20.fw-normal.text-secondary.mb-4 Over the past two months, Qatar has expanded bilateral trade and investment ties across multiple regions. New agreements and delegations advanced cooperation with Turkey, Sweden, Hong Kong, the U.S., and Malaysia, with the latter seeing trade volume rise of nearly 80%. The Qatar-Hong Kong merchandise trade corridor alone topped $1.6 billion last year. Qatar’s $500 billion U.S. investment push by its sovereign wealth fund also underscores its growing international economic footprint.
            p.fs-20.fw-normal.text-secondary.mb-4 The Ministry of Commerce and Industry announced plans to launch 38 new e-services in 2025, signaling an ambitious digital transformation. In a tech-forward move, Qatar also partnered with Microsoft to introduce AI-powered virtual assistants for improved citizen services.
            p.fs-20.fw-medium.text-secondary.mb-4 Steady Economic Performance and Investor Momentum
            p.fs-20.fw-normal.text-secondary.mb-4 Qatar recorded $2.7 billion in FDI for 2024, driven by resilient non-oil sectors. Oxford Economics projects steady non-energy growth through 2025, with a sharper pickup expected in 2026. Complementing this, Invest Qatar unveiled $1 billion in incentives, reinforcing the country’s competitiveness, which was recognized in the 2025 Global Competitiveness Report, where Qatar ranked among the global leaders for the first time.
